- Story & Context: In the deepest reach of the terminal, the recluse Vörglath obsessively tuned his Hydra guitar to the frequency of a dying polar bear's final exhaled gasp. He ignored the flickering power grids and the frantic knocks at his blast-door, lost in the ritual of repeating a single, dissonant chord until his knuckles bled. "Your heartbeat is a borrowed rhythm I’ve already claimed" he whispered into his microphone, his voice distorted into a gutteral, metallic croak that perfectly mirrored the jagged 8-string djent riffs beneath him.
