Track 3: The Last Departure Was A Lie
- Story & Context: History records the terminal as abandoned, but the walls still groan with the rhythmic tectonic shifts of the hidden, hibernating machines. Kora, a scout, found the frozen timetable scribbled in blood on the floorboards, marking a departure time that does not exist in the linear calendar. She realizes too late that the hibernation rhythm is the only music that remains, a final, beautiful burial for a world that refused to stay asleep. "Burn the tickets, the engine is already part of the ice" she sang as the final, cavernous drop dragged the track into an endless, silence-filled sustain.
